    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-6929",
      "problem": "The graph of $y=f'(x),$ the derivative of $f(x),$ is shown below. Given that $f(0)=0,$ sketch a possible graph of $y=f(x).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14200695/assets/ef91945c0b2261785677c4c8ba7e6d202f62bc6c2da20a213bcba03cbcad8556.png)",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that critical points of $y=f(x)$ occur when $f'(x)=0$ or $f'(x)$ does not exist. In our case, there is one critical point:\n\n$$\nx=-2\n$$\n\nAlso, we have the following: \n\n- If $f'(x) > 0$ then $f(x)$ is increasing.\n\n- If $f'(x) <          0$ then $f(x)$ is decreasing.\n\nWe can now summarize the information from the graph in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $(-\\infty,-2)$ | $-2$ | $(-2,\\infty)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f'$ | $-$ | $0$ | $+$ |\n| $f$ | $\\searrow$ | $\\textrm{min}$ | $\\nearrow$ |\n\nLet's now sketch the graph of $y=f(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n- First, we draw the critical point. Consider the vertical line $x=-2.$\n\n- Since we are told that $f(0)=0,$ we can draw that point on the graph.\n\n- Since $f(x)$ is increasing $\\nearrow$ on $(-2,\\infty),$ the point at $x=-2$ must be lower than the point at $x=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14200695/assets/4b599481e7a73ec38b6f0f627b1b9a551c65e6cd3875b3789f0e7ebfa03eb786.png)\n\n- Next, we consider the behavior of $y=f(x)$ in the neighborhood of the critical point:\n\n- Since $f(x)$ is decreasing $\\searrow$ on $(-\\infty,-2)$ and increasing $\\nearrow$ on $(-2,\\infty)$, the graph of $y=f(x)$ goes up to the left and to the right of $x=-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14200695/assets/1ae0017fd07d6e9fa04f233ca31ab89a07260a5dbc5557e4c8ae35ff91d61f43.png)\n\n- Finally, by connecting and extending the existing parts with a smooth curve, we obtain a possible graph of $y=f(x)\\mathbin{:}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14200695/assets/c215907aa0cc156e92ab3b6710d844e774df3149656fc2f71f27ee01db87382e.png)",
